From f383b786f03718566e0cfd150afc5cefbb47a8f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius S <39998+winding-lines@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:24:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Request bodies: default Content-Type can be turned off;
 empty PUT/POST/PATCH send Content-Length: 0

HttpClient.default_content_type (still "application/json" by default)
is the Content-Type given to a body sent without one; "" sends none.
Object stores keep the request's Content-Type as the object's, so a
binary upload was stored as application/json.

An empty POST, PUT or PATCH went out with no Content-Length at all,
which RFC 9110 8.6 asks for and S3 requires (411 Length Required).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 http_client.mojo | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 test_client.mojo | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test_server.py   |  1 +
 3 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

